the interactive map/huds system:
it uses screen lananguage which is similar to java swing. it sets up the ui elements and their positions.
which makes the hud and map interactive as well as update based on game states.

each interacted room:
the map is split into rooms which is created through a factory design pattern.
the rooms are templates that can be inherited and overridden to create new rooms with similar structure.
and then to enter a room, a command pattern is used to execute the jump to the room.
each room may contain a piece of the story or a mini game or another system.

courtyard:
Event manager to handle the different events that can occur in the courtyard.
each event is queued up using the event queue design pattern. this is set up so different events can
occure after one another base on the day system criteria.
each event condition and story block is stored in its day and mapped through a dictionary data structure for the day condition.
(might change from dictionary to just using a json.) 

shop system:
in the shop room, it uses enums for the type of items and a dictionary to map out
the condition and properties of each item. as well as when it is unlocked.
it uses renpy screen language to notify and update the item state. 

day system: this is the core system for every other system to function.
such as the event queue. it relies on the specific day and time to trigger certain events.
the day system uses tuples to store the day and time.
each interaction increase the time counter which after 3 increments, it changes the day.

